# E2E Testing Conventions

Ported from `.claude/rules/nest-e2e.md`, scoped identically across the six NestJS backend
services.

- Files: `test/<area>.e2e-spec.ts`; run with `npm run test:e2e` against the REAL Postgres from
  `infra/docker-compose.yml` (services that own a database only — `bff` has none)
- Build the app from `AppModule` via `Test.createTestingModule`

## Bootstrap config is NOT inherited

`main.ts` settings (global `/api` prefix, versioning, pipes) do not apply to the test app:

- Routes are unprefixed in e2e: request `/health`, not `/api/v1/health`
- Re-enable the pipe manually, mirroring main.ts:
  `app.useGlobalPipes(new ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, transform: true }))`

## Data isolation

- Unique test values with a run prefix, e.g. `` const emailPrefix = `e2e-${Date.now()}` ``
- Clean up in `afterAll` before `await app.close()` for any records the test created

## Style

- `import request from 'supertest'` — default import (namespace import is not callable under
  esModuleInterop)
- Type response bodies explicitly, e.g. `const body = res.body as HealthCheckResult`
- Cover the full flow including error codes (409 duplicate, 400 validation, 404 missing) once a
  feature module exists — `test/app.e2e-spec.ts` is currently the only spec, covering `/health`
